// _n1_listener_close_test -- the N1-exit listener-keep-alive + graceful-shutdown guard (adversary Finding #1).
// main parks in tcp_accept on a listener that NEVER receives a connection. Two things must hold:
//   (1) KEEP-ALIVE: the carrier must NOT idle-exit while main is parked on the listener (pre-fix it broke
//       after a ~10ms poll -> main abandoned, no PASS). The 200ms wait below only completes if the carrier
//       stays alive for the listener waiter.
//   (2) CLOSE-WAKE: a background task closes the listener at +200ms. tcp_close must WAKE the parked accept
//       (it cannot rely on select(), which reports a closed fd as EBADF and wakes nobody) so accept retries,
//       hits the closed-fd error, and returns -1 -- rather than the carrier spinning on the dead fd forever
//       (the HANG the listener keep-alive would otherwise introduce).
// MUST TERMINATE under kill-on-timeout. Run at N=1 (the keep-alive path) AND N=4.
fn closer(srv: int, done)
    sleep(200)            // let main reach tcp_accept and park first
    tcp_close(srv)        // wakes main's parked accept with a closed fd
    send(done, 1)

fn main()
    let srv = tcp_listen(19011)
    let done = channel()
    spawn closer(srv, done)
    let conn = tcp_accept(srv)   // parks ~200ms (keep-alive), then woken by the close -> -1
    recv(done)
    assert(conn < 0, "parked accept returned an error after the listener closed (got " + str(conn) + ")")
    print("PASS listener_close: parked accept stayed alive ~200ms then woke with " + str(conn) + " on close (no idle-exit, no hang)")
